{"authored" [{"question" "q-2420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int x{5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-2420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x{5}^{x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={5}^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}-\\int \\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{x{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}-\\int \\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}-\\frac{{5}^{x}}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5))^{2}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-2420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2405a0d59b762ca246d05602433b2bd1e5d035f108323f2b9b81df964df831d5" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-2420" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-2420" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(1-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-2420" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(\\frac{1}{x}-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-2420" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-2420" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-1)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-2420" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-2420" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe, substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 6x\\cdot {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =6x\\cdot (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x{e}^{-3x}+2\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-2x{e}^{-3x}+2\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114287" "field" nil "attribute" "q