ategory" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114287" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{3{e}^{-3x}}{2}+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114287" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114287" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114297" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114297" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114297" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2405a0d59b762ca246d05602433b2bd1e5d035f108323f2b9b81df964df831d5" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{6}+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/state.json" "file_sha256" "5023efbc4a5ac1d8d85aa770504141b2f6adffb0be8461a7c7b6183c8600186b" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/example-491.json" "file_sha256" "7c46823a076f27418f687c1c57f0be26c1c0d58db148bd07e8215baee597f933" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv' \\, \\textrm{d}x= uv - \\int vu' \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle  \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle  \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{7x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}-\\int \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}\\int {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}(\\frac{{e}^{7x}}{7})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{49}{e}^{7x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/example-491.json" "file_sha256" "7c46823a076f27418f687c1c57f0be26c1c0d58db148bd07e8215baee597f933" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int x \\cos{2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/example-492.json" "file_sha256" "6ea45868b53e6a7ef46cd6a099a1f9edf4ee7fd285ddd7f1dc86b89a549281ab" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x= uv- \\int vu'\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x \\cos{2x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/example-492.json" "file_sha256" "6ea45868b53e6a7ef46cd6a099a1f9edf4ee7fd285ddd7f1dc86b89a549281ab" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6209" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/5} x\\sin(5x) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/example-6209.json" "file_sha256" "873e4784b82e098e69e17d1c87e19a6fff599f58729fd44e363879ddeff1d870" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6209" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x) & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-\\int (-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+{\\frac{1}{5}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})|}_{0}^{\\pi /5} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)]+[\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[-\\frac{\\pi }{25}\\cdot (-1)+0]+[0-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/example-6209.json" "file_sha256" "873e4784b82e098e69e17d1c87e19a6fff599f58729fd44e363879ddeff1d870" "basis" 1141 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009414/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49682" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031626/state.json" "file_sha256" "3ddbf1755e389721b5699fd87b6d64f8c9041b32617e322cc23dfb2983b00e34" "basis" 1215 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031626/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49682" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & ⇒ & v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x){|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =2[\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & +2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =2[-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}]+2[0-0] \\\\  & =2(-2\\pi )+0 \\\\  & =-4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031626/state.json" "file_sha256" "3ddbf1755e389721b5699fd87b6d64f8c