jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-114297" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-114297" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f12dea770497d297247a2cb79ecdcc904740445870ab69551b14378c475ea87c"} {"question" "q-114297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-114297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{6}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C"] ["math" "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-114297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-14449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int 5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-14449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=5x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=5 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 5x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =5x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\cdot 5\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+5\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-14449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f12dea770497d297247a2cb79ecdcc904740445870ab69551b14378c475ea87c"} {"question" "q-14449" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-14449" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+C"] ["math" "5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-14449" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-14437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-14437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-14437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f12dea770497d297247a2cb79ecdcc904740445870ab69551b14378c475ea87c"} {"question" "q-14437" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-14437" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-14437" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-114299" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-114299" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\int \\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-114299" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f12dea770497d297247a2cb79ecdcc904740445870ab69551b14378c475ea87c"} {"question" "q-114299" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-114299" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{4}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{6}+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{8}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{8}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{2}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-114299" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{8}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-49676" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate  ${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-49676" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & ⟹\\,v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}+{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-[\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})] \\\\  & +[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})] \\\\  & =[\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot 0-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}]+[1-\\frac{1}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{12}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-49676" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f12dea770497d297247a2cb79ecdcc904740445870ab69551b14378c475ea87c"} {"question" "q-49676" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-49676" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\pi }{12}+\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\pi }{6}-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{12}+1"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{12}+\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{6}-\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-49676" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{12}+\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-49684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1/3}2x{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-49684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{3x} & ⇒ & v=\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3})\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}2x{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\frac{2}{3}x{e}^{3x}|}_{0}^{1/3}-\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}{e}^{3x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{2}{3}x{e}^{3x}|}_{0}^{1/3}-{\\frac{2}{9}{e}^{3x}|}_{0}^{1/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3(1/3)}-0\\cdot {e}^{3\\cdot 0}]-\\frac{2}{9}[{e}^{3(1/3)}-{e}^{3\\cdot 0}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\frac{e}{3}-0]-\\frac{2}{9}[e-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{2e}{9}-\\frac{2e}{9}+\\frac{2}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-49684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f12dea770497d297247a2cb79ecdcc904740445870ab69551b14378c475ea87c"} {"question" "q-49684" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-49684" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2e}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{9e}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-49684" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{9}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-346870" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}2x{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-346870" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{x} & ⇒ & v={e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot {e}^{x}-\\int {e}^{x}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2x{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2x{e}^{x}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x{e}^{x}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}-2{e}^{x}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2(1\\cdot {e}^{1}-0\\cdot {e}^{0})-2({e}^{1}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =2e-2(e-1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-346870" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f12dea770497d297247a2cb79ecdcc904740445870ab69551b14378c475ea87c"} {"question" "q-346870" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-346870" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-114330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-114330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=5x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=5 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x) & ⇒ & v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 5x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =5x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}\\cdot 5\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /5} \\\\  & =[\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5})-0\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & +\\frac{1}{5}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =(0-0)+\\frac{1}{5}(-1-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-114330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f12dea770497d297247a2cb79ecdcc904740445870ab69551b14378c475ea87c"} {"question" "q-114330" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-114330" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{5}"] ["math" "-\\frac{6}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-114330" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{2}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-49682" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-49682" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & ⇒ & v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x){|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =2[\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & +2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =2[-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}]+2[0-0] \\\\  & =2(-2\\pi )+0 \\\\  & =-4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-49682" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f12dea770497d297247a2cb79ecdcc904740445870ab69551b14378c475ea87c"} {"question" "q-49682" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-49682" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4\\pi "] ["math" "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "-\\pi "] ["math" "2\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "q-49682" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4\\pi "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/state.json" "file_sha256" "21e3e196aff192f4c4050903a8272d9961cccd1bdfd206a269712b9a6f763352"} {"question" "e-491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/example-491.json" "file_sha256" "7c46823a076f27418f687c1c57f0be26c1c0d58db148bd07e8215baee597f933"} {"question" "e-491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv' \\, \\textrm{d}x= uv - \\int vu' \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle  \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle  \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{7x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}-\\int \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}\\int {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}(\\frac{{e}^{7x}}{7})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{49}{e}^{7x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/example-491.json" "file_sha256" "7c46823a076f27418f687c1c57f0be26c1c0d58db148bd07e8215baee597f933"} {"question" "e-492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int x \\cos{2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/example-492.json" "file_sha256" "6ea45868b53e6a7ef46cd6a099a1f9edf4ee7fd285ddd7f1dc86b89a549281ab"} {"question" "e-492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x= uv- \\int vu'\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x \\cos{2x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/example-492.json" "file_sha256" "6ea45868b53e6a7ef46cd6a099a1f9edf4ee7fd285ddd7f1dc86b89a549281ab"} {"question" "e-6209" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/5} x\\sin(5x) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/example-6209.json" "file_sha256" "873e4784b82e098e69e17d1c87e19a6fff599f58729fd44e363879ddeff1d870"} {"question" "e-6209" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x) & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-\\int (-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+{\\frac{1}{5}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})|}_{0}^{\\pi /5} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)]+[\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[-\\frac{\\pi }{25}\\cdot (-1)+0]+[0-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038125/example-6209.json" "file_sha256" "873e4784b82e098e69e17d1c87e19a6fff599f58729fd44e363879ddeff1d870"}] "usage" {"q-114297" [] "q-114299" [] "q-2420" [] "q-49682" [] "e-491" [] "q-114287" [] "e-6209" [] "q-14449" [] "q-49684" [] "q-14437" [] "q-346870" [] "e-492" []} "basis" 1294 "retractions" [[17592186064794 :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{1/3}2xe^{3x}dx$."] [17592186064794 :question/worked-solution "Using $u=2x$ and $dv=e^{3x}\\,dx$, an antiderivative is $\\frac23xe^{3x}-\\frac29e^{3x}$. Hence\n$$\\int_0^{1/3}2xe^{3x}\\,dx\n=\\left[\\frac23xe^{3x}-\\frac29e^{3x}\\right]_0^{1/3}\n=0-\\left(-\\frac29\\right)=\\frac29.$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186061229 17592186061230 17592186061231 17592186061232 17592186061233 17592186063275 17592186063276 17592186063277 17592186063278 17592186063279 17592186289107 17592186289108 17592186289109 17592186289110 17592186289111 17592186289128 17592186289129 17592186289130 17592186289131 17592186289132 17592186289170 17592186289171 17592186289172 17592186289173 17592186289174 17592186293237 17592186293238 17592186293239 17592186293240 17592186293241 17592186296529 17592186296530 17592186296531 17592186296532 17592